      "VELOCITY.txns_per_minute": "transactions-per-minute is count * 60 / W, an exact deterministic rescaling of vel_{entity}_count_{w}s which is already emitted. Emitting both would be the same quantity under two names (perfectly collinear for the Logistic Regression baseline). Set features.emit_rate_per_min=true in configuration to emit it."
    },
    "documented_deviations": {
      "CONTEXT.merchant_window_txn_count": "mer_txn_count_{w}s is merchant-side window volume. It is not itself a locked Merchant Pattern item; it is emitted because MERCHANT.related_entities is a raw count of related devices/IPs at the current merchant and is uninterpretable without the merchant's own window volume as scale. Not a dispersion measure and deliberately NOT merchant->card entropy (that direction was the audited error)."
    },
